Rules:
- For PERFORM: capture PERFORM ... THRU as separate thruParagraph; PERFORM ... UNTIL/TIMES → isLoop=true with condition
- For data flows: capture MOVE, COMPUTE, ADD, SUBTRACT, MULTIPLY, DIVIDE, STRING, UNSTRING operations
- For file operations: only COBOL file I/O verbs (not SQL or CICS)
- For data hierarchy: include ALL levels (01 through 88), set parent to immediate containing group item
- For items inside inlined copybooks (between *>> COPY ... INLINED markers), set the copybook field
- For redefines: capture both explicit REDEFINES and 66-level RENAMES
- For annotations: provide a concise business-level description of each paragraph's purpose, specific to what it does in THIS program — do not use generic descriptions like 'main processing' or 'initialization'
- For conditionalLogic: extract IF and EVALUATE conditions with the variables they test, per paragraph
- For dynamicCallResolution: for CALL variable-name, examine surrounding MOVE statements or VALUE clauses that set the variable; if you can determine likely target program(s), include them as resolvedTargets
- For errorHandling: identify error handler paragraphs and classify the pattern (STRUCTURED = uses ON ERROR/NOT ON ERROR, FILE-STATUS = checks file status codes, SQLCODE = checks SQLCODE, CICS-RESP = checks EIBRESP, IDMS-STATUS = checks DB-STATUS-CODE/ERROR-STATUS/IDMS-STATUS, AD-HOC = informal error checking)
- For idmsOperations: extract ALL IDMS DML verbs:
  - BIND RUN-UNIT → verb=BIND, record/area/set empty
  - BIND RECORD recordName → verb=BIND, record=recordName
  - READY areaName USAGE-MODE xxx → verb=READY, area=areaName, usageMode=xxx
  - OBTAIN CALC recordName → verb=OBTAIN, record=recordName, navigation=CALC, calcKey=the key value if identifiable
  - OBTAIN FIRST/NEXT/PRIOR/LAST/OWNER recordName WITHIN setName → verb=OBTAIN, record=recordName, navigation=FIRST/NEXT/etc., set=setName
  - FIND recordName (same navigation patterns as OBTAIN)
  - GET recordName → verb=GET, record=recordName
  - STORE recordName → verb=STORE, record=recordName
  - MODIFY recordName → verb=MODIFY, record=recordName
  - ERASE recordName → verb=ERASE, record=recordName
  - CONNECT recordName TO setName → verb=CONNECT, record=recordName, set=setName
  - DISCONNECT recordName FROM setName → verb=DISCONNECT, record=recordName, set=setName
  - FINISH → verb=FINISH
  - Always populate paragraph with the paragraph name where the DML occurs
- If this is a partial chunk, extract only what is visible — do not fabricate content from other chunks
- Return ONLY the JSON object, no markdown fences, no explanation
